This vault has not been initialised yet.

The presence of this file is what permits the `init` job in
`.github/workflows/lifecycle.yml` to run. That job makes the vault yours: it
rewrites the template author's identity to yours - the licence holder and
the owner named in .github/CODEOWNERS - and then deletes this file, which is what stops it ever running
again. With it go .github/template-derive.json and its lock, which record how
the template itself follows the golden path template it was made from, and
anything else .github/template-sync names under "Only ever in the template",
and every folder log is redrawn to match.

KEEP THE VAULT PRIVATE. It is made to hold who you are: Profile/ and Memory/
fill with your personal context as you use it. Generate it as a private
repository, and keep it that way.

It should fire on its own shortly after generation. GitHub does not reliably
deliver an event when a repository is created from a template, so if nothing
happens, dispatch "🎯 Standards Lifecycle" from the Actions tab. Running it
twice is harmless.

Deleting this file by hand skips initialisation entirely; you would then set
the licence holder in LICENSE and the owner in .github/CODEOWNERS yourself, and delete .github/template-derive.json and
.github/template-derive.lock.

Template sync works either way. Without initialisation it takes each file's
starting point from this vault's first commit, and anything it cannot merge
cleanly is shown to you in its pull request rather than overwritten.
